Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 18:36:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] fix: wire experience facts/sections into the Lara
 translation pipeline
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

syncSectionTranslations/syncFactTranslations existed but nothing ever
called them, and getFullExperiences() never read back
experience_sections_translations/experience_facts_translations — so
the "facts" (duration, departure point, etc.) and "sections" ("what's
included", etc.) shown on the featured experience card were always
English regardless of locale, same root cause already fixed for
title/description.

- /api/translate-experience now also accepts { sectionId } / { factId }
  and syncs that row via Lara.
- experienceRepository.ts triggers that sync from
  create/updateExperienceSection and create/updateExperienceFact,
  mirroring the existing updateExperience() pattern.
- getFullExperiences(locale) now localizes each fact's label/value and
  each section's title/description via getLocalizedField, same as the
  top-level experience fields.
---
 src/app/api/translate-experience/route.ts |  78 ++++++++++++++---
 src/lib/supabase/experienceRepository.ts  | 102 +++++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 159 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

